// A stamp whose ceiling names more than the arrangement under it can hold.
//
// The direction the other fixtures do not drive. A ceiling is a statement of
// consent, so a word nothing reaches is refused as dead config — which is what
// keeps the narrow body on `config/deployment.brenn`'s click page honest: the
// day `@demo-panel`'s `DemoPage` starts conferring `publish`, a bundle-side
// change made by someone who is not the deployer, this document compiles and
// this gate is what says so.
//
// Stamped under the operator rather than under a principal, so the body is the
// whole ceiling and the refusal is about it alone.
use @demo-panel::*;

new demo: DemoPage(slug = "demo", skin = "bench") {
  grants = [dom, log, page-dom, ports, publish];
}
